210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (A single-node Wazuh environment was successfully deployed using Docker Engine on Kali Linux and configured through the command line. The setup includes monitoring of an agent system for security events. VirusTotal integration enables automated file hash analysis for malware detection, while AlienVault OTX provides threat intelligence to identify malicious IP addresses. MITRE ATT&CK mapping helps in understanding attacker behavior by linking events to known tactics and techniques. File Integrity Monitoring ensures system integrity by detecting unauthorized changes, and Active Response automates mitigation actions.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (The system was tested using simulated threats such as EICAR test files and malicious IP lookups. The results confirm that the integrations work effectively, improving detection accuracy and enabling faster response to security incidents.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
